<article class="env-definition" id="01G5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01G5">Definition <span data-tag="01G5">25.3.3</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Assume $\mathcal{C}$ has fibre products. Let $X \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$ be an object of $\mathcal{C}$. A <em>hypercovering of $X$</em> is a simplicial object $K$ of $\text{SR}(\mathcal{C}, X)$ such that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The object $K_0$ is a covering of $X$ for the site $\mathcal{C}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
For every $n \geq 0$ the canonical morphism 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  K_{n + 1} \longrightarrow (\text{cosk}_ n \text{sk}_ n K)_{n + 1}  \]
</div>
<p>
 is a covering in the sense defined above. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>